    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0818" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/12–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paddock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-24T13:00:00-05:00">December 24,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Urtels 233<anchor n="34" xml:id="d708-f1"/> and 235.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d708-f2"/> Not planned send couriers each <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smolny</hi> trip. Once 3 months believed adequate. Gleysteen should not
                    enter Communist Manchuria unless permission enter such territory and travel
                    Mukden obtained either in Dairen or at border.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
